IMPORT prelude

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore) -- offers of shares and other securities (Part 13 Division 1): the prospectus
-- requirement (s 240(1), (7)), the exemptions for small offers (s 272A), private placements (s 272B), offers to
-- institutional investors (s 274), and offers to accredited investors and other relevant persons or for $200,000 or more
-- (s 275(1), (1A), (2)); and who is an accredited investor (s 4A(1)(a), (1A)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SFA2001.txt. Section numbers are the BODY's. THE ARRANGEMENT TABLE IS ONE LINE OUT OF STEP
-- HERE: it puts "Offer made to institutional investors" against 273 and "Offer made to accredited investors" against 274;
-- in the body s 273 is "Offer made under certain circumstances", s 274 is the institutional-investor exemption and s 275
-- is the accredited-investor exemption. The ledger's "ss 272A-275" is right as a range.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0285 (Haziq scenario, event h042): a private company issues shares to one angel
-- investor for $500,000, and four years later to a venture fund for $5,000,000 -- must a prospectus be registered for
-- either, and is the angel an accredited investor?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 272 (no-consideration issues); s 273 (take-overs, rights issues, employee schemes and the other listed
-- circumstances); s 276 (resale of securities first acquired under s 274 or 275); ss 277-280 (offer information
-- statements, international debentures, government offers, ATMs); s 257 (allotment with a view to resale deemed a
-- prospectus), which every exemption expressly leaves in force; s 272A(8) and the resale notification's own conditions;
-- the "closely related offer" factors (ss 272A(6), 272B(4), prescribed by the Authority); s 4A(1)(a)(iii) and (iv) and the
-- Authority's power in s 4A(2) to modify the definitions; amounts the Authority may prescribe in place of those in the Act
-- (the encoding uses the Act's figures); Subdivision (1A) and s 240AA (product highlights sheets); the Companies Act 1967
-- rules for private companies; any opt-in or opt-out by an accredited investor, which the Act does not mention.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Securities and Futures Act 2001 -- offers of securities and their exemptions`

§§ `4A(1)(a) and (1A) -- accredited investor`

-- s 4A(1)(a)(i): an individual "(A) whose net personal assets EXCEED in value $2 million ...; (B) whose financial assets (net
-- of any related liabilities) EXCEED in value $1 million ...; or (C) whose income in the preceding 12 months is NOT LESS
-- THAN $300,000". Each is "or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount".
-- s 4A(1A): for (A), "the value of the individual's primary residence -- (a) is to be calculated by deducting any outstanding
-- amounts in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the residence from the estimated fair market value of the
-- residence; and (b) is taken to be the lower of ... (i) the value calculated under paragraph (a); (ii) $1 million."
--
-- Nothing in s 4A makes the size of an investment relevant: a $500,000 cheque does not make its writer an accredited
-- investor. The tests are wealth and income.
DECLARE Individual HAS
    `net personal assets other than the primary residence` IS A NUMBER
    `estimated fair market value of the primary residence` IS A NUMBER
    `credit secured on the primary residence` IS A NUMBER
    `financial assets net of related liabilities` IS A NUMBER
    `income in the preceding 12 months` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counted value of the primary residence` `the individual` MEANS
    IF (`the individual`'s `estimated fair market value of the primary residence` MINUS `the individual`'s `credit secured on the primary residence`) GREATER THAN 1000000
    THEN 1000000
    ELSE `the individual`'s `estimated fair market value of the primary residence` MINUS `the individual`'s `credit secured on the primary residence`

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net personal assets of` `the individual` MEANS
    `the individual`'s `net personal assets other than the primary residence` PLUS `the counted value of the primary residence` `the individual`

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is an accredited investor` IF
        `the net personal assets of` `the individual` GREATER THAN 2000000
    OR  `the individual`'s `financial assets net of related liabilities` GREATER THAN 1000000
    OR  `the individual`'s `income in the preceding 12 months` AT LEAST 300000

-- s 4A(1)(a)(ii): "a corporation with net assets EXCEEDING $10 million in value ... as determined by (A) the most recent
-- audited balance sheet ... or (B) where the corporation is not required to prepare audited accounts regularly, a balance
-- sheet ... certified by the corporation ... [dated] within the preceding 12 months".
GIVEN `net assets on the balance sheet` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a corporation with these net assets is an accredited investor` IF
    `net assets on the balance sheet` GREATER THAN 10000000

§§ `275(2) -- relevant person`

-- s 275(2) "relevant person" means "(a) an accredited investor; (b) a corporation the sole business of which is to hold
-- investments and the entire share capital of which is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited
-- investor; (c) a trustee of a trust the sole purpose of which is to hold investments and each beneficiary of which is an
-- individual who is an accredited investor; (d) an officer ... of the person making the offer (such person being an
-- entity) or a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of that officer ...; or (e) a spouse, parent, brother,
-- sister, son or daughter of the person making the offer (such person being an individual)."
GIVEN `sole business is holding investments` IS A BOOLEAN, `every shareholder is an individual accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding corporation is a relevant person` IF
    `sole business is holding investments` AND `every shareholder is an individual accredited investor`

§§ `272B(5) -- counting the persons offered`

-- s 272B(5)(a): an offer "to an entity or to a trustee is treated as an offer to a single person, provided that the entity or
-- trust is not formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities ... which are the subject of the offer"; (b): if
-- it IS so formed, the offer is "treated as an offer to the equity owners, partners or members of that entity, or to the
-- beneficiaries of the trust". (c): joint owners count as a single person.
GIVEN `formed primarily to acquire these securities` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of its equity owners or beneficiaries` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the persons counted for an offer to an entity` `formed primarily to acquire these securities` `number of its equity owners or beneficiaries` MEANS
    IF `formed primarily to acquire these securities` THEN `number of its equity owners or beneficiaries` ELSE 1

§§ `The offer`

-- The common conditions. ss 272A(1)(c), 272B(1)(b), 275(1)(a) and (1A)(b): no "advertisement making an offer or calling
-- attention to the offer or intended offer" (an information memorandum or a descriptive document prepared for the offerees
-- is not an advertisement: ss 272A(10)(d), 275(2)). ss 272A(1)(d), 272B(1)(c), 275(1)(b) and (1A)(c): no selling or
-- promotional expenses "other than those incurred for administrative or professional services, or by way of commission or
-- fee for services rendered by" a licensed or exempt dealer (Singapore or foreign). ss 272A(1)(e), 272B(1)(d), 275(1)(c) and
-- (1A)(d): no prospectus for the offer registered, or if one was, it has expired under s 250 or the Authority was told
-- beforehand that the exemption is relied on. One flag stands for each of these.
DECLARE Offer HAS
    `amount raised by this offer` IS A NUMBER
    `amount raised under section 272A in the 12 months, counting this offer` IS A NUMBER
    `persons offered under section 272B in the 12 months, counting this offer` IS A NUMBER
    `minimum consideration per transaction on the offer terms` IS A NUMBER
    `is a personal offer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the section 272A statement and resale notification were given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by an advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `selling or promotional expenses beyond those permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registered prospectus stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offeree is an institutional investor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offeree is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offeree is another relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offeree acquires as principal` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the common conditions are met` IF
        (NOT `the offer`'s `accompanied by an advertisement`)
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `selling or promotional expenses beyond those permitted`)
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `a registered prospectus stands in the way`)

§§ `272A -- small offers`

-- s 272A(1): the prospectus Subdivisions "do not apply to PERSONAL offers of securities ... by a person if -- (a) the total
-- amount raised by the person from such offers within any period of 12 months DOES NOT EXCEED -- (i) $5 million"; (b) in
-- respect of each offer the offeree is given the written statement "This offer is made in reliance on the exemption under
-- section 272A(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not made in or accompanied by a prospectus that is registered
-- by the Monetary Authority of Singapore." and a written notification restricting resale; and (c) to (e) as above.
-- (3): a personal offer is one that "(a) may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made; and (b) is made to a person
-- who is likely to be interested in that offer, having regard to" previous contact, connection or indication of interest.
-- (5): offers in the same 12 months in reliance on s 272A(1) (or s 302B(1)) by the same issuer, and closely related offers,
-- are added together. (4): the amount raised includes uncalled amounts on partly-paid shares and conversion amounts.
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 272A small-offer exemption applies` IF
        `the offer`'s `is a personal offer`
    AND `the offer`'s `amount raised under section 272A in the 12 months, counting this offer` AT MOST 5000000
    AND `the offer`'s `the section 272A statement and resale notification were given`
    AND `the common conditions are met` `the offer`

§§ `272B -- private placement`

-- s 272B(1): the prospectus Subdivisions "do not apply to offers of securities ... that are made by a person if -- (a) the
-- offers are made to NO MORE THAN 50 persons within any period of 12 months"; and (b) to (d) as above.
-- (3): counted are the persons offered securities of the same entity "within that period in reliance on the exemption under
-- this section", and closely related offers. Offers made under s 274 or s 275 are not counted.
--
-- Fifty is allowed; fifty-one is not. The ledger's "fewer than 50" is one short.
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 272B private-placement exemption applies` IF
        `the offer`'s `persons offered under section 272B in the 12 months, counting this offer` AT MOST 50
    AND `the common conditions are met` `the offer`

§§ `274 -- institutional investors`

-- s 274: the prospectus Subdivisions "do not apply to an offer of securities ... (whether or not they have been previously
-- issued) made to an institutional investor." No other condition. s 4A(1)(c) lists institutional investors; among them
-- "(xiv) a holder of a capital markets services licence" and "(xxiv) a pension fund, or collective investment scheme,
-- whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere".
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 274 institutional-investor exemption applies` IF
    `the offer`'s `the offeree is an institutional investor`

§§ `275(1) and (1A) -- accredited investors, relevant persons, and $200,000`

-- s 275(1): the prospectus Subdivisions "do not apply to an offer of securities ... where the offer is made to a RELEVANT
-- PERSON, if" (a) to (c) as above.
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 275(1) relevant-person exemption applies` IF
        (`the offer`'s `the offeree is an accredited investor` OR `the offer`'s `the offeree is another relevant person`)
    AND `the common conditions are met` `the offer`

-- s 275(1A): nor "to an offer of securities ... to a person who acquires the securities ... AS PRINCIPAL ... if -- (a) the
-- offer is on terms that the securities ... may only be acquired at a consideration of NOT LESS THAN $200,000 (or its
-- equivalent in a foreign currency) for each transaction, whether such amount is to be paid for in cash or by exchange of
-- securities ... or other assets"; and (b) to (d) as above. (4): the Authority may substitute another amount by order in the
-- Gazette.
--
-- No status test at all: an investor who is not accredited may take shares for $200,000 or more without a prospectus.
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 275(1A) large-transaction exemption applies` IF
        `the offer`'s `the offeree acquires as principal`
    AND `the offer`'s `minimum consideration per transaction on the offer terms` AT LEAST 200000
    AND `the common conditions are met` `the offer`

§§ `240 -- the prospectus requirement`

-- s 240(1): "A person must not make an offer of securities ... unless the offer -- (a) is made in or accompanied by a
-- prospectus ... (i) that is prepared in accordance with section 243; (ii) a copy of which ... is lodged with the Authority;
-- and (iii) that is registered by the Authority". s 2(1): "securities" means "(a) shares ...".
-- Each exemption above disapplies Subdivision (2), which contains s 240.
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `some exemption applies` IF
        `the section 272A small-offer exemption applies` `the offer`
    OR  `the section 272B private-placement exemption applies` `the offer`
    OR  `the section 274 institutional-investor exemption applies` `the offer`
    OR  `the section 275(1) relevant-person exemption applies` `the offer`
    OR  `the section 275(1A) large-transaction exemption applies` `the offer`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a registered prospectus is required` IF
    NOT `some exemption applies` `the offer`

-- s 240(7): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- to a fine not exceeding $150,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a
-- continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- continues after conviction."
GIVEN `days of continuing offence after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an offer without a prospectus` `days of continuing offence after conviction` MEANS
    150000 PLUS 15000 TIMES `days of continuing offence after conviction`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum prison term in years for an offer without a prospectus` MEANS 2
